          "text": "The module-level `signal` is just `default_namespace.signal` bound method, so validation in `Namespace.signal` covers both. Need to raise TypeError before dict lookup/modification, even if the key exists. Check `isinstance(name, str)` — str subclasses pass via isinstance. Empty string fine.\n\nEdit:\n\n```python\n        if not isinstance(name, str):\n            raise TypeError(\"name must be a string\")\n\n        if name not in self:\n```\n\nWait — careful: `name not in self` on a dict — for non-hashable names that would raise; for e.g. int names it would work. We need TypeError before lookup. Add the check first.",
