          "type": "text",
          "text": "The change is complete. I added a type check at the start of `Namespace.signal` in `src/blinker/base.py`:\n\n```python\nif not isinstance(name, str):\n    raise TypeError(f\"name must be a string, not {type(name).__name__}\")\n\nif name not in self:\n    self[name] = NamedSignal(name, doc)\n\nreturn self[name]\n```\n\nKey points:\n- The check runs **before** any dictionary lookup or modification, so non-string names are rejected even if that key already exists in the namespace.\n- `isinstance` accepts `str` subclasses and the empty string.\n- The module-level `signal` helper is defined as `signal = default_namespace.signal` (a bound method), so it gets the same validation with no additional changes.\n- Signal identity for repeated names, docstring handling, and receiver dispatch are untouched.",
